{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>The flesh was yet between their teeth.</b> It had not yet reached the point at which they would loathe it." "<b>Before it was cut off.</b> The allotted period of a month had not yet arrived." "<b>And HaShem struck the people.</b> Among the ones who craved, who asked for meat to test — and they were stricken through their own testing. For He did not say 'and you shall eat a month of days' except concerning those who wept without craving, who said, 'Why did we come out of Egypt?' — and they wept in their illness, as it says (Numbers 11:20), 'and it shall be to you for loathing.'"], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:39:26.954690Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}